☠ MORTAL FRETS — The Fretboard Slayer
A retro arcade-style guitar fretboard training game, inspired by Mortal Kombat. Train your fretboard knowledge across 4 identification modes, compete on a global leaderboard, and earn the FLAWLESS VICTORY.
🎮 Play Now

Game Modes
All modes play as rounds of 10 questions. Score = total errors (fewer is better). Tiebreaker: fastest time.
Identification
ModeWhat you seeWhat you doNote IDA dot on the fretboard (frets 0–12, all strings)Press the correct note nameInterval IDTwo dots — R (root, red) and a second dot within ±3 frets / ±2 stringsPress the correct interval (m2 → P8)Chord IDA chord voicing within ±2 frets / ±2 strings of the root, one note per stringPress the correct chord typeScale IDA full scale pattern in a 5-fret box, R = rootPress the correct scale name
Construction modes (Note Play, Interval Construction, Chord Construction, Scale Construction) — coming in v2.0.

Rules

Wrong answer → stay on the same question, retry. Timer keeps running.
Mercy button ☠ → activates after 2 wrong answers on the same question. Hold to reveal the answer on the fretboard; release to hide it and retry. Resets on each new question.
Variety → same note / interval / chord / scale type appears at most twice per round; the exact same question never repeats.
Notation → toggle between A-B-C and Do-Re-Mi at any time.
Box selection → Chord ID and Scale ID let you work on a specific 5-fret box or use 💀 KHAOS for a random box each question.


Scoring
ErrorsResult0⚡ FLAWLESS VICTORY1–2EXCELLENT FIGHTER3–5SKILLED WARRIOR6–10FIGHT HARDER11–19FINISH HIM20+FATALITY

Deploy on GitHub Pages

Fork or clone this repository
Make sure the main file is named index.html
Go to Settings → Pages → Source: Deploy from branch → main → / (root)
Your game will be live at https://yourusername.github.io/mortal-frets/ within a minute or two


Global Leaderboard (Firebase)
By default the game stores scores in localStorage (local, per-browser). To enable a real global leaderboard:

Go to console.firebase.google.com
Create a new project (or reuse an existing one)
Add a Realtime Database → Start in test mode
Copy your project config (the firebaseConfig object from Project Settings → Your apps)
Open index.html and replace the FB_CONFIG block near the top of the <script>:

jsconst FB_CONFIG = {
  apiKey:      "your-api-key",
  authDomain:  "your-project.firebaseapp.com",
  databaseURL: "https://your-project-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com",
  projectId:   "your-project-id",
};

Save and redeploy. Scores are now stored globally under leaderboards/{mode}/ in your database.


Security note: Before going public, set Firebase rules to allow only writes (no reads of other users' data beyond the leaderboard query), and consider rate-limiting. For a small personal project, test mode is fine.


Tech Stack

Pure HTML / CSS / JavaScript — no framework, no build step
Web Audio API for note synthesis
SVG fretboard rendered in-browser
Firebase Realtime Database for global leaderboard (optional)
Press Start 2P + Rajdhani via Google Fonts


Music Theory Coverage
Notes: all 12 chromatic notes, frets 0–12, all 6 strings (standard tuning E A D G B e)
Intervals: m2 · M2 · m3 · M3 · P4 · TT · P5 · m6 · M6 · m7 · M7 · P8
Chords: Major · minor · Augmented · Diminished · Maj7 · Dom7 · min7 · ø7 (half-dim) · °7 (dim7)
Scales: Major · Natural Minor · Harmonic Minor · Melodic Minor · Whole-Half Diminished · Half-Whole Diminished

